<Base title="About Lot & Lounge and how we source prices" description="How Lot & Lounge checks airport parking rates and lounge access: official sources only, dated checks, and no invented prices or lounge names." path="about/">
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>About Lot &amp; Lounge</h1>
    <p>Lot &amp; Lounge answers two boring but expensive travel questions for each airport: <em>where should I leave the car, and what will it really cost?</em> and <em>which lounge can I actually get into?</em></p>
    <h2>How we source</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Parking rates come from the airport operator's own website or tariff sheet. Each page shows the date we last checked and links every source.</li>
      <li>Lounge lists come from the airport's official directory and the lounge operators' own pages (for example Priority Pass airport pages).</li>
      <li>"Total cost" examples are our own arithmetic from published rates (for example 7 × the daily maximum). Your actual charge depends on entry and exit times and the rate posted at the gate.</li>
      <li>If we can't verify something, we leave it out or tell you to check with the airport. We never guess prices, hours or lounge names.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>What we don't do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We don't recommend credit cards or other financial products.</li>
      <li>We aren't affiliated with any airport, airline or lounge operator.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Spotted something out of date? The official source always wins, and we update pages as rates change.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
